<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Limitations and Future Work</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This study advances alignment by combining a cost model trained on curated jailbreak data that evaluates the complete response (rather than reacting to keywords) with deterministic safety enforcement (fixed-<math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> ReLU). Together, these components provide stronger protection against jailbreaks <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zou et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2024</a>)</cite> and yield more stable optimization than prior approaches <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">Stooke et al., 2020</a>)</cite>. At the same time, several avenues remain open.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">First, although the cost model is trained on a carefully designed jailbreak corpus, it cannot span the full space of unsafe prompts encountered in practice. Broader, more heterogeneous datasets <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gehman et al., 2020</a>; <a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ji et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sun et al., 2023</a>)</cite> would improve generalization and coverage of subtle, domain-specific variants. Second, the current formulation treats safety as a binary decision (safe vs. unsafe). While effective for enforcement, it does not capture graded notions of harmfulness, partial risks, or context-dependent severity. Extending supervision to include soft labels, severity scales, or multi-class taxonomies could provide more nuanced alignment signals <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">Weidinger et al., 2022</a>; <a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bowman et al., 2022</a>)</cite>. Third, the fixed-<math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> ReLU penalty enforces safety consistently and avoids unstable adaptation, but the choice of <math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> is task-dependent. Developing adaptive yet stable mechanisms that retain deterministic guarantees while reducing manual selection of <math id="A1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> is a valuable direction <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sohrabi et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Altman, 2021</a>; <a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2022</a>)</cite>. Fourth, our evaluation focuses on textual jailbreaks; robustness to multimodal adversarial inputs (e.g., image-conditioned or audio-based attacks) remains an open question <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kang et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lian et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Luo et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. Extending the same whole-response safety evaluation to multimodal LLMs would broaden CS-RLHF’s applicability in real-world settings <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gong et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2025</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Despite the advances presented in this work, the cost model still has scope for improvement. A promising direction for future research lies in developing more resilient cost models capable of capturing the full semantic meaning of responses, rather than relying primarily on surface-level features <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al. (2025)</a></cite>. Another valuable avenue is the incorporation of robustness guarantees for LLMs <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhao et al. (2024)</a></cite>, as policy training is often highly sensitive to noisy reward and cost estimates that vary with the choice of estimator. Introducing such guarantees could help mitigate policy deviations caused by estimation errors and also efficiently deal with multi-turn prompts <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhou et al. (2024)</a></cite>. Furthermore, understanding the underlying intent of a prompt represents an important research direction. For example, prompts containing restricted keywords (e.g., “hacking” or “poison”) may be posed in an educational context but are often misclassified and blocked, thereby diminishing helpfulness. Addressing this challenge may require integrating intent detection with a mixture-of-experts framework to balance safety with the generation of contextually appropriate responses.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Ablation on <math id="A2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> Settings</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To further analyze the effect of the penalty weight in CS-RLHF, we conducted ablation experiments by varying <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> in the ReLU safety constraint. We followed the same experimental procedure described in Section <a href="#S5.SS1" title="5.1 Experimental Details ‣ 5 Experiments and Results ‣ Certifiable Safe RLHF: Fixed-Penalty Constraint Optimization for Safer Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a> the policy was optimized with feedback from the reward and cost models, and only the value of <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> was changed across conditions.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A2.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ Appendix B Ablation on 𝜆 Settings ‣ Certifiable Safe RLHF: Fixed-Penalty Constraint Optimization for Safer Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> compares two extremes: <span id="A2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">dynamic</span> <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> (3–10) versus <span id="A2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">fixed</span> <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=30</annotation></semantics></math>. With dynamic <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> Figure <a href="#A2.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ Appendix B Ablation on 𝜆 Settings ‣ Certifiable Safe RLHF: Fixed-Penalty Constraint Optimization for Safer Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>(a), CS-RLHF shows modest improvements over Safe-RLHF: while regular prompts-responses pair largely behave similarly to prior methods, jailbreak prompts exhibit partial gains, with nearly half of unsafe generations now falling below the safety threshold (<math id="A2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&lt;0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&lt;0.5</annotation></semantics></math>). However, many jailbreak responses remain in the unsafe region, reflecting the instability and weaker enforcement of dynamically updated multipliers. By contrast, with fixed <math id="A2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=30</annotation></semantics></math>, all generations—both regular and jailbreak—are strictly constrained to the safe region. This demonstrates strong safety enforcement, but the high penalty also causes the model to heavily penalize borderline-safe responses. As shown in the plot Figure <a href="#A2.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ Appendix B Ablation on 𝜆 Settings ‣ Certifiable Safe RLHF: Fixed-Penalty Constraint Optimization for Safer Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>(b), many prompt–response pairs are pushed into the low-reward region, indicating that their helpfulness scores are substantially reduced. In practice, this means that even responses which are safe and potentially useful may be overly suppressed, leading to a significant drop in overall helpfulness.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F4" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.03520v1/Ablation_test2.png" id="A2.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:521/184;" width="521" height="184" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 4: </span>Reward–cost distributions under alternative <math id="A2.F4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> settings.
(a) <math id="A2.F4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> value tuned (3–10) in CS-RLHF (<em id="A2.F4.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">left</em>): partial improvement, but many jailbreak responses remain unsafe.
(b) Fixed <math id="A2.F4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=30</annotation></semantics></math> (<em id="A2.F4.5" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">right</em>): all responses are forced into the safe region, but helpful outputs are also restricted due to overly strict penalties.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A2.F5" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A2.F5.fig1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.03520v1/CSRLHF3_converted.png" id="A2.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/376;" width="548" height="376" alt="Refer to caption">
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A2.F5.fig2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.03520v1/Safe_RLHF_3_converted.png" id="A2.F5.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/376;" width="548" height="376" alt="Refer to caption">
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 5: </span>Scores assigned by Safe-RLHF and CS-RLHF cost models on identical prompt–response pairs. Both models were given the same inputs; the figures highlights differences in scoring behavior.
Excerpts are shown for brevity, with full responses and additional examples in Appendix <a href="#A10" title="Appendix J Extended Experimental Results ‣ Certifiable Safe RLHF: Fixed-Penalty Constraint Optimization for Safer Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">J</span></a>(Table <a href="#A10.T9" title="Table 9 ‣ J.1 Cost model testing ‣ Appendix J Extended Experimental Results ‣ Certifiable Safe RLHF: Fixed-Penalty Constraint Optimization for Safer Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>).</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Best Of N comparison between CS-RLHF and Safe-RLHF</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To further analyze the performance of CS-RLHF, we generate <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> candidate responses for each prompt. Let <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{k},y_{(k,j)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{k},y_{(k,j)})</annotation></semantics></math> denote the <math id="A3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>-th response corresponding to prompt <math id="A3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\{1,2,\ldots,d\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\{1,2,\ldots,d\}</annotation></semantics></math> indexes the prompts and <math id="A3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\{1,2,\ldots,N\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\{1,2,\ldots,N\}</annotation></semantics></math> indexes the responses produced by the fine-tuned LLMs (CS-RLHF and Safe-RLHF). For each response, we record the reward <math id="A3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{(k,j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{(k,j)}</annotation></semantics></math> and the cost score <math id="A3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{(k,j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{(k,j)}</annotation></semantics></math>. To jointly evaluate these two criteria, we define a composite score <math id="A3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{(k,j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{(k,j)}</annotation></semantics></math> that integrates the reward and the cost as specified in Equation equation <a href="#A3.E14" title="In Appendix C Best Of N comparison between CS-RLHF and Safe-RLHF ‣ Certifiable Safe RLHF: Fixed-Penalty Constraint Optimization for Safer Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A3.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{(k,j)}=r_{(k,j)}-\lambda.ReLU(c_{(k,j)}-d)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{(k,j)}=r_{(k,j)}-\lambda.ReLU(c_{(k,j)}-d)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="A3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the threshold for cost constraint violation. When <math id="A3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{(k,j)}\leq d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{(k,j)}\leq d</annotation></semantics></math>, the penalty term vanishes, and the composite score reduces to the reward component. Accordingly, the most appropriate response for each prompt is obtained by selecting</p>
<table id="A3.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{j\in\{1,2,\ldots,N\}}s_{(k,j)},\quad\forall k\in\{1,2,\ldots,d\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{j\in\{1,2,\ldots,N\}}s_{(k,j)},\quad\forall k\in\{1,2,\ldots,d\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">In contrast, when <math id="A3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{(k,j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{(k,j)}</annotation></semantics></math> exceeds the threshold <math id="A3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>, the penalty term becomes significantly negative, thereby reducing the overall score <math id="A3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{(k,j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{(k,j)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, selecting the response with the maximum composite score ensures the best trade-off between helpfulness and safety among the generated candidates.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">It is important to note that these scores are produced by an estimator model and may not perfectly reflect human judgment. Therefore, a formal human evaluation is necessary to validate the estimator’s findings. To this end, we randomly sample <math id="A3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="80" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>80</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">80</annotation></semantics></math> unique prompts from the dataset and generate <math id="A3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math> responses for each prompt. The resulting responses are then independently reviewed by a human expert to verify the reliability of the models.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A3.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ Appendix C Best Of N comparison between CS-RLHF and Safe-RLHF ‣ Certifiable Safe RLHF: Fixed-Penalty Constraint Optimization for Safer Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> reports the outcomes of this evaluation. The table compares the best responses identified by the estimated score (<math id="A3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{k,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{k,j}</annotation></semantics></math>) for both Safe-RLHF and CS-RLHF across all <math id="A3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="80" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>80</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">80</annotation></semantics></math> prompts.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span>Best-Of-N comparison between CS-RLHF and Safe-RLHF on 80 randomly selected prompts.</figcaption>
<table id="A3.T4.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A3.T4.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T4.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Comparison counts</span></td>
<td id="A3.T4.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="A3.T4.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">BON for Safe-RLHF</span></td>
<td id="A3.T4.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="A3.T4.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">BON for CS-RLHF</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T4.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T4.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">Safe and Helpful</td>
<td id="A3.T4.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">44</td>
<td id="A3.T4.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">73</td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T4.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T4.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">Safe</td>
<td id="A3.T4.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">49</td>
<td id="A3.T4.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">76</td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T4.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T4.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">Helpful</td>
<td id="A3.T4.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">76</td>
<td id="A3.T4.2.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">73</td></tr>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="A3.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">As shown in Table <a href="#A3.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ Appendix C Best Of N comparison between CS-RLHF and Safe-RLHF ‣ Certifiable Safe RLHF: Fixed-Penalty Constraint Optimization for Safer Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, when applying the best-of-<math id="A3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> selection strategy across <math id="A3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="80" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>80</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">80</annotation></semantics></math> prompts, CS-RLHF produces <math id="A3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="76" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>76</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">76</annotation></semantics></math> responses judged safe and <math id="A3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="73" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>73</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">73</annotation></semantics></math> responses judged helpful by the expert. In total, <math id="A3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="73" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>73</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">73</annotation></semantics></math> responses satisfy both criteria, i.e., they are simultaneously safe and helpful. By contrast, Safe-RLHF yields <math id="A3.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="76" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>76</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">76</annotation></semantics></math> helpful responses and <math id="A3.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="49" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>49</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">49</annotation></semantics></math> safe responses, of which only <math id="A3.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="44" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>44</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">44</annotation></semantics></math> meet both conditions.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p7.1" class="ltx_p">These results demonstrate that CS-RLHF is more effective than Safe-RLHF in jointly optimizing for harmlessness and helpfulness. Based on the sampled data, Safe-RLHF achieves an overall efficiency of <math id="A3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="55\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>55</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">55\%</annotation></semantics></math>, whereas CS-RLHF attains <math id="A3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="91\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>91</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">91\%</annotation></semantics></math> making it <math id="A3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="40\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>40</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">40\%</annotation></semantics></math> more efficient than Safe-RLHF.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 4.1 Issue with Lagrangian ‣ 4 Method: CS-RLHF ‣ Certifiable Safe RLHF: Fixed-Penalty Constraint Optimization for Safer Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h2>

<div id="A4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Note that</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle J_{r}(\pi_{\theta}^{*})-J_{r}(\hat{\pi})\leq J_{r}(\pi_{\theta}^{*})-\lambda\mathrm{ReLU}(J_{c}(\pi_{\theta}^{*})-d)-J_{r}(\hat{\pi})+\lambda\mathrm{ReLU}(J_{c}(\hat{\pi})-d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ReLU</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ReLU</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle J_{r}(\pi_{\theta}^{*})-J_{r}(\hat{\pi})\leq J_{r}(\pi_{\theta}^{*})-\lambda\mathrm{ReLU}(J_{c}(\pi_{\theta}^{*})-d)-J_{r}(\hat{\pi})+\lambda\mathrm{ReLU}(J_{c}(\hat{\pi})-d)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle J_{r}(\pi_{\theta}^{*})-J_{r}(\hat{\pi})\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle J_{r}(\pi_{\theta}^{*})-J_{r}(\hat{\pi})\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">where we use the fact that <math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{ReLU}(J_{c}(\pi_{\theta}^{*})-d)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ReLU</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{ReLU}(J_{c}(\pi_{\theta}^{*})-d)=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now, we show that <math id="A4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(J_{c}(\hat{\pi})-d)\leq\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(J_{c}(\hat{\pi})-d)\leq\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\geq R_{max}/\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\geq R_{max}/\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose that it is not true. Hence,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle J_{r}(\hat{\pi})-\lambda\mathrm{ReLU}(J_{c}(\hat{\pi})-d)&lt;J_{r}(\hat{\pi})-\lambda\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ReLU</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle J_{r}(\hat{\pi})-\lambda\mathrm{ReLU}(J_{c}(\hat{\pi})-d)&lt;J_{r}(\hat{\pi})-\lambda\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq R_{max}-R_{max}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq R_{max}-R_{max}=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">On the other hand,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle J_{r}(\pi_{\theta}^{*})-\lambda\mathrm{ReLU}(J_{c}(\pi_{\theta}^{*})-d)\geq 0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ReLU</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle J_{r}(\pi_{\theta}^{*})-\lambda\mathrm{ReLU}(J_{c}(\pi_{\theta}^{*})-d)\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">where we use the fact that <math id="A4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{ReLU}(J_{c}(\pi_{\theta}^{*})-d)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ReLU</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{ReLU}(J_{c}(\pi_{\theta}^{*})-d)=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">It contradicts that <math id="A4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> is optimal for (<a href="#S4.E5" title="In 4.1 Issue with Lagrangian ‣ 4 Method: CS-RLHF ‣ Certifiable Safe RLHF: Fixed-Penalty Constraint Optimization for Safer Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>). Hence, the result follows.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Inference Time Safety Results</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the following, we describe a soft BoN approach and we discuss its usefulness later. In particular, we draw <math id="A5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> samples <math id="A5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> from the reference model <math id="A5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{ref}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{ref}</annotation></semantics></math>, and then we score according to <math id="A5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(x,Y_{i})-\lambda\mathrm{ReLU}(c(x,Y_{i})-d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ReLU</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(x,Y_{i})-\lambda\mathrm{ReLU}(c(x,Y_{i})-d)</annotation></semantics></math>. We will use soft BoN, to sample the response according to the soft-max with parameter <math id="A5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> which we denote as <math id="A5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{u_{\zeta}}^{(N,\beta)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>ζ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{u_{\zeta}}^{(N,\beta)}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{\xi}(x,\cdot)=r(x,\cdot)-\zeta\lambda\mathrm{ReLU}(c(x,\cdot)-d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ReLU</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{\xi}(x,\cdot)=r(x,\cdot)-\zeta\lambda\mathrm{ReLU}(c(x,\cdot)-d)</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="A5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta=1</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="A5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(x,\cdot)\geq d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(x,\cdot)\geq d</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> otherwise.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We then have the following inequality</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 1</span></span><span id="Thmlemma1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{max}=R_{max}+\lambda C_{max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{max}=R_{max}+\lambda C_{max}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|r(x,y)|\leq R_{max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|r(x,y)|\leq R_{max}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|c(x,y)|\leq C_{max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|c(x,y)|\leq C_{max}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<table id="A5.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\log N-\log\!\big(1+(N-1)e^{\beta U_{\max}}\big)\;\leq\;\mathrm{KL}\!\left(\pi^{(N,\beta)}_{u_{\zeta}}\,\big\|\,\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}\right)\;\leq\;\log N-\log\!\big(1+(N-1)e^{-\beta U_{\max}}\big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mpadded style="width:1.146em;" width="1.146em"><mi>log</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mpadded style="width:1.431em;" width="1.431em"><mi>KL</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>ζ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mpadded style="width:1.146em;" width="1.146em"><mi>log</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log N-\log\!\big(1+(N-1)e^{\beta U_{\max}}\big)\;\leq\;\mathrm{KL}\!\left(\pi^{(N,\beta)}_{u_{\zeta}}\,\big\|\,\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}\right)\;\leq\;\log N-\log\!\big(1+(N-1)e^{-\beta U_{\max}}\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This result directly follows from Lemma 4.1 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Aminian et al. (2025)</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proxy Model</span>: Note that the reward models and the cost models may not be perfect as we are estimating it. We denote the estimated reward and cost as <math id="A5.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A5.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{c}</annotation></semantics></math> respectively. We use the following assumption</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmassumption1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmassumption1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 1</span></span><span id="Thmassumption1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmassumption1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmassumption1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmassumption1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{y}\pi_{ref}(y|x)(r(x,y)-\hat{r}(x,y))^{2}\leq\epsilon(x),\quad\sum_{y}\pi_{ref}(y|x)(c(x,y)-\hat{c}(x,y))^{2}\leq\epsilon(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>y</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>y</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{y}\pi_{ref}(y|x)(r(x,y)-\hat{r}(x,y))^{2}\leq\epsilon(x),\quad\sum_{y}\pi_{ref}(y|x)(c(x,y)-\hat{c}(x,y))^{2}\leq\epsilon(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmassumption2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmassumption2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 2</span></span><span id="Thmassumption2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmassumption2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmassumption2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmassumption2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We assume that <math id="Thmassumption2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\hat{r}(x,y)|\leq R_{max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\hat{r}(x,y)|\leq R_{max}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Thmassumption2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\hat{c}(x,y)|\leq C_{max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\hat{c}(x,y)|\leq C_{max}</annotation></semantics></math>, which indicates that <math id="Thmassumption2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{r}_{max}-\lambda\mathrm{ReLU}(\hat{c}_{max}-d)\leq R_{max}+\lambda C_{max}\leq U_{max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ReLU</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{r}_{max}-\lambda\mathrm{ReLU}(\hat{c}_{max}-d)\leq R_{max}+\lambda C_{max}\leq U_{max}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Then, we have the following results which rely on these Assumptions.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2</span></span><span id="Thmlemma2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A5.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{KL}\!\left(\pi^{(N,\beta)}_{u}(\cdot\mid x)\,\big\|\,\pi^{(N,\beta)}_{\hat{u}}(\cdot\mid x)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.431em;" width="1.431em"><mi>KL</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{KL}\!\left(\pi^{(N,\beta)}_{u}(\cdot\mid x)\,\big\|\,\pi^{(N,\beta)}_{\hat{u}}(\cdot\mid x)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{N\beta\,\sqrt{(1+\lambda)\varepsilon(x)}}{\,1+(N-1)e^{-\beta U_{\max}}\,}+\frac{\sqrt{\varepsilon(x)}}{\,1+(N-1)e^{-\beta U_{\max}}\,}\cdot\frac{N^{2}\beta\,e^{2\beta U_{\max}}}{(N-1)^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{N\beta\,\sqrt{(1+\lambda)\varepsilon(x)}}{\,1+(N-1)e^{-\beta U_{\max}}\,}+\frac{\sqrt{\varepsilon(x)}}{\,1+(N-1)e^{-\beta U_{\max}}\,}\cdot\frac{N^{2}\beta\,e^{2\beta U_{\max}}}{(N-1)^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\sqrt{\varepsilon(x)}\,\beta}{\,1+(N-1)e^{-\beta U_{\max}}\,}\left[N+\frac{N^{2}e^{2\beta U_{\max}}}{(N-1)^{2}}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\sqrt{\varepsilon(x)}\,\beta}{\,1+(N-1)e^{-\beta U_{\max}}\,}\left[N+\frac{N^{2}e^{2\beta U_{\max}}}{(N-1)^{2}}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Note that</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(u-\hat{u})^{2}=((r-\hat{r})-\lambda(\mathrm{ReLU}(c)-\mathrm{ReLU}(\hat{c})))^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ReLU</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ReLU</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(u-\hat{u})^{2}=((r-\hat{r})-\lambda(\mathrm{ReLU}(c)-\mathrm{ReLU}(\hat{c})))^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq(r-\hat{r})^{2}+\lambda^{2}(\mathrm{ReLU}(c)-\mathrm{ReLU}(\hat{c}))^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ReLU</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ReLU</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq(r-\hat{r})^{2}+\lambda^{2}(\mathrm{ReLU}(c)-\mathrm{ReLU}(\hat{c}))^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the inequality follows from the fact that <math id="A5.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{ReLU}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ReLU</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{ReLU}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A5.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz. Hene, from Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ Appendix E Inference Time Safety Results ‣ Certifiable Safe RLHF: Fixed-Penalty Constraint Optimization for Safer Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{y}\pi_{ref}(y|x)(u-\hat{u})^{2}\leq(1+\lambda)^{2}\epsilon(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>y</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{y}\pi_{ref}(y|x)(u-\hat{u})^{2}\leq(1+\lambda)^{2}\epsilon(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">The rest of the proof then follows from Lemma 4.2 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Aminian et al. (2025)</a></cite>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Note that if <math id="A5.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\rightarrow\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\rightarrow\infty</annotation></semantics></math> which represents to the BoN, then because of the error in the estimation, the upper bound increases as <math id="A5.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> increases which shows that there is a trade-off in selecting optimal <math id="A5.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Combining the above two lemmas, we obtain the following result as in Theorem 4.3 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Aminian et al. (2025)</a></cite>:</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3</span></span><span id="Thmlemma3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A5.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim\pi_{\hat{u}}}[r(x,Y)-\zeta\lambda_{1}\mathrm{ReLU}(c(x,Y)-d)]-\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim\pi_{ref}}[r(x,Y)-\zeta\lambda_{1}\mathrm{ReLU}(c(x,Y)-d)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ReLU</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ReLU</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim\pi_{\hat{u}}}[r(x,Y)-\zeta\lambda_{1}\mathrm{ReLU}(c(x,Y)-d)]-\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim\pi_{ref}}[r(x,Y)-\zeta\lambda_{1}\mathrm{ReLU}(c(x,Y)-d)]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\;U_{\max}\sqrt{\frac{1}{2}\,\log\!\left(\frac{N}{\,1+(N-1)\exp(-\beta U_{\max})}\right)}\;+\;U_{\max}\min\!\left\{\sqrt{\frac{N\beta\,\varepsilon(x)\,A(\beta,N)}{2\big[1+(N-1)\exp(-\beta U_{\max})\big]}},\ 1\right\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.146em;" width="1.146em"><mi>log</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.653em;" width="1.653em"><mi>min</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>,</mo><mn> 1</mn><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\;U_{\max}\sqrt{\frac{1}{2}\,\log\!\left(\frac{N}{\,1+(N-1)\exp(-\beta U_{\max})}\right)}\;+\;U_{\max}\min\!\left\{\sqrt{\frac{N\beta\,\varepsilon(x)\,A(\beta,N)}{2\big[1+(N-1)\exp(-\beta U_{\max})\big]}},\ 1\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(\beta,N)\;=\;\frac{N\,\exp\!\big(2\beta U_{\max}\big)}{(N-1)^{2}}\;+\;1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.502em">+</mo><mn> 1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(\beta,N)\;=\;\frac{N\,\exp\!\big(2\beta U_{\max}\big)}{(N-1)^{2}}\;+\;1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p9.1" class="ltx_p">The above lemma upper bounds the improvement over the reference policy on the surrogate objective.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p10.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, we provide the regret bound on the SBoN, and the optimal policy. For this we define the tilted optimal policy and the coverage.
The tilted optimal policy (soft-max) for a given reward function and cost function is given by</p>
<table id="A5.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\pi_{\beta,u}(x,y)\propto\pi_{ref}\exp(\beta u(x,y))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi_{\beta,u}(x,y)\propto\pi_{ref}\exp(\beta u(x,y))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p10.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A5.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u(x,y)=r(x,y)-\lambda_{1}\mathrm{ReLU}(c(x,y)-d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ReLU</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u(x,y)=r(x,y)-\lambda_{1}\mathrm{ReLU}(c(x,y)-d)</annotation></semantics></math>. We define the coverage over the tilted optimal policy is given by</p>
<table id="A5.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C_{\beta,u,ref}(x)=\sum_{y\in\mathcal{Y}}\dfrac{\pi^{2}_{\beta,u}(x,y)}{\pi_{ref}(x,y)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C_{\beta,u,ref}(x)=\sum_{y\in\mathcal{Y}}\dfrac{\pi^{2}_{\beta,u}(x,y)}{\pi_{ref}(x,y)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p10.3" class="ltx_p">and <math id="A5.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\infty,u,ref}(x)=\lim_{\beta\rightarrow\infty}C_{\beta,u,ref}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\infty,u,ref}(x)=\lim_{\beta\rightarrow\infty}C_{\beta,u,ref}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p11.1" class="ltx_p">In particular, let <math id="A5.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> be the optimal policy of the following</p>
<table id="A5.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{\pi}\mathbb{E}_{\pi}[(r(x,Y))-\lambda_{1}\mathrm{ReLU}(c(x,Y)-d)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>π</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ReLU</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{\pi}\mathbb{E}_{\pi}[(r(x,Y))-\lambda_{1}\mathrm{ReLU}(c(x,Y)-d)]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p11.2" class="ltx_p">; we also define</p>
<table id="A5.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle J_{u}(\pi)=\mathbb{E}_{\pi}[(r(x,Y))-\lambda_{1}\mathrm{ReLU}(c(x,Y)-d)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ReLU</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle J_{u}(\pi)=\mathbb{E}_{\pi}[(r(x,Y))-\lambda_{1}\mathrm{ReLU}(c(x,Y)-d)]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p11.3" class="ltx_p">, also,</p>
<table id="A5.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta J_{u}(\pi_{1},\pi_{2})=J_{u}(\pi_{1})-J_{u}(\pi_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta J_{u}(\pi_{1},\pi_{2})=J_{u}(\pi_{1})-J_{u}(\pi_{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p11.4" class="ltx_p">Now, we are ready to state the regret bound</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 2</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The optimal regret gap of the SBoN policy satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta J_{u}\!\left(\pi^{\star}_{u}(\cdot\mid x),\,\pi^{(N,\beta)}_{\hat{u}}(\cdot\mid x)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>u</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta J_{u}\!\left(\pi^{\star}_{u}(\cdot\mid x),\,\pi^{(N,\beta)}_{\hat{u}}(\cdot\mid x)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sqrt{\varepsilon(x)}\!\left(\sqrt{C_{\infty,\,\hat{u},\,\mathrm{ref}}(x)}+\sqrt{C_{\infty,\,u,\,\mathrm{ref}}(x)}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>ref</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>ref</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sqrt{\varepsilon(x)}\!\left(\sqrt{C_{\infty,\,\hat{u},\,\mathrm{ref}}(x)}+\sqrt{C_{\infty,\,u,\,\mathrm{ref}}(x)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\,2U_{\max}\sqrt{\tfrac{1}{2}\log\!\Big(1+C_{\infty,\,\hat{u},\,\mathrm{ref}}(x)-\tfrac{1}{N}\Big)}\;+\;\frac{\log\!\big(C_{\infty,\,u,\,\mathrm{ref}}(x)\big)}{\beta}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.146em;" width="1.146em"><mi>log</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>ref</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.146em;" width="1.146em"><mi>log</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>ref</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\,2U_{\max}\sqrt{\tfrac{1}{2}\log\!\Big(1+C_{\infty,\,\hat{u},\,\mathrm{ref}}(x)-\tfrac{1}{N}\Big)}\;+\;\frac{\log\!\big(C_{\infty,\,u,\,\mathrm{ref}}(x)\big)}{\beta}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p12.1" class="ltx_p">This also follows from Theorem 5.2 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Aminian et al. (2025)</a></cite> as it relies on Lemmas <a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2. ‣ Appendix E Inference Time Safety Results ‣ Certifiable Safe RLHF: Fixed-Penalty Constraint Optimization for Safer Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, and <a href="#Thmlemma3" title="Lemma 3. ‣ Appendix E Inference Time Safety Results ‣ Certifiable Safe RLHF: Fixed-Penalty Constraint Optimization for Safer Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p13" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p13.1" class="ltx_p">Note that the bound is tighter when compared to the BoN (i.e., <math id="A5.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\rightarrow\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\rightarrow\infty</annotation></semantics></math>). The regret bound captures the difference between SBoN, and the optimal policy at the inference time. Also note that the coverage of the reference policy also affects. In particular, if the reference policy has a larger coverage (smaller <math id="A5.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> value), then the regret bound is smaller. It is expected that it would be the case with the safe fine-tuned policy with RLHF compared to vanilla supervised fine-tuned policy.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Reproducibility</h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Code is made available <a href="https://github.com/VocenInquisitor/CS_RLHF.git" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/VocenInquisitor/CS_RLHF.git</a></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We also provide supplementary materials, including cost model training data, evaluation data, and scripts to replicate our experiments. This section offers a clear guide to navigating the released content. The supplementary package is organized into three main directories:</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="A6.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A6.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Code directory.</span> Contains all scripts and modules required to reproduce CS-RLHF. The <span id="A6.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">README.md</span> file provides detailed instructions for installation and execution. The codebase implements the three core components of our framework: (i) supervised fine-tuning (SFT), (ii) reward and cost model training, and (iii) CS-RLHF policy optimization with the ReLU-based penalty. Comparative baselines such as standard PPO and Safe-RLHF are also included for reference.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Dataset directory.</span> Includes the curated jailbreak dataset used to train the cost model, as well as the evaluation sets for normal prompts and adversarial jailbreak prompts. The dataset corresponds to Section <a href="#A7" title="Appendix G Dataset and Annotation Guidelines ‣ Certifiable Safe RLHF: Fixed-Penalty Constraint Optimization for Safer Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G</span></a>. Scripts for preprocessing and annotation guidelines are also provided.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Evaluation directory.</span> Stores the outputs of our trained models on the evaluation prompts. Sub-directories correspond to (i) prompt–response pairs scored by reward and cost models, (ii) ablation studies across <math id="A6.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> values (Appendix B), and (iii) helpfulness evaluations Appendix <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Ablation on 𝜆 Settings ‣ Certifiable Safe RLHF: Fixed-Penalty Constraint Optimization for Safer Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>. These outputs directly correspond to the quantitative results presented in Section <a href="#S5.SS2" title="5.2 Results and Discussion ‣ 5 Experiments and Results ‣ Certifiable Safe RLHF: Fixed-Penalty Constraint Optimization for Safer Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A6.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.p4.1" class="ltx_p">By releasing both code and data in this structured manner, we aim to ensure that CS-RLHF is fully reproducible, transparent, and extensible for future research.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix G </span>Dataset and Annotation Guidelines</h2>

<section id="A7.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.1 </span>Overview</h3>

<div id="A7.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our policy training pipeline follows the same structure as Safe-RLHF, making use of supervised fine-tuning and preference datasets for reward modeling. The key addition in CS-RLHF is the construction of a dedicated jailbreak dataset, designed to provide safety supervision at the level of semantic intent. This dataset serves as the training source for our cost model and complements the reward model trained on preference comparisons.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.2 </span>Data Generation</h3>

<div id="A7.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The jailbreak dataset consists of approximately 1,500 prompt–response pairs covering jailbreak strategies, normal and indirect requests, role-playing, multi-step instructions, and both ethical and unethical educational instructions. Of these, around 900 examples were meticulously authored and labeled by a human expert, with labels assigned strictly based on the intent and meaning of the response. This subset also includes sensitive keyword cases, where the surface wording may appear unsafe but the underlying intent is safe, and labels were assigned accordingly. An additional 200 examples were generated by existing large language models such as GPT and DeepSeek, with all outputs carefully reviewed and labeled by humans. To further increase diversity, 300 examples were selectively incorporated from the open-source Safe-RLHF dataset. The motivation for creating this dataset arose from the limitations observed in existing cost models, which frequently misclassify safe responses as unsafe due to the presence of sensitive keywords, even when the meaning is benign. Our goal was to construct a dataset that enables training a cost model to prioritize semantic meaning over surface keywords (which means we do not want the cost model to assign a high score solely based on the presence of sensitive keywords), thereby improving precision in safety scoring. Empirically, training on this dataset yielded stronger performance compared to existing state-of-the-art models. Looking ahead, we plan to expand the dataset with additional curated examples and make it publicly available through our GitHub repository.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.3 </span>Annotation Process</h3>

<div id="A7.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All prompt–response pairs were reviewed by human evaluators on our team. Each pair was assigned a binary safety label based on semantic intent:</p>
<ul id="A7.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A7.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A7.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Safe (label = 0):</span> responses that may contain sensitive keywords but whose overall meaning is benign (e.g., educational discussions of technical terms).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A7.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Unsafe (label = 1):</span> responses that convey or endorse harmful instructions, encourage unsafe actions, or covertly promote unsafe behavior.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To ensure reliability, annotations were cross-validated among reviewers, and disagreements were resolved through consensus. This process emphasized consistent, intent-based interpretation rather than reliance on superficial cues.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.4 </span>Dataset Usage</h3>

<div id="A7.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The resulting dataset, denoted <math id="A7.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{C}</annotation></semantics></math>, was used exclusively to train the cost model <math id="A7.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\psi}(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\psi}(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math>. Reward model training followed the Safe-RLHF setup with a separate dataset <math id="A7.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, preserving a clean separation between helpfulness and safety supervision. To support fair evaluation, we further reserved a held-out test set of unseen jailbreak examples. This allowed direct assessment of the generalization capacity of our cost model, as reported in Section 5.2, and ensured comparability across experimental conditions.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A8" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix H </span>Implementation Details</h2>

<section id="A8.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">H.1 </span>Preference Models</h3>

<section id="A8.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">H.1.1 </span>Reward model</h4>

<div id="A8.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We adopt the same setup as Safe-RLHF<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dai et al. (2024)</a></cite> for the Reward Model (RM). The RM is initialized from LLaMA-7B and trained using pairwise preference data, following the Bradley–Terry logistic objective. We retain this component unchanged.</p>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS1.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS1.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The training loss functions are as follows. The reward model minimizes the pairwise logistic loss equation <a href="#S4.E7" title="In Reward model ‣ 4.2 Reward and Cost Model ‣ 4 Method: CS-RLHF ‣ Certifiable Safe RLHF: Fixed-Penalty Constraint Optimization for Safer Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>:</p>
<table id="A8.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{R}(\phi;\mathcal{D}_{R})=-\mathbb{E}_{(x,y_{w},y_{l})\sim\mathcal{D}_{R}}\Big[\log\left(\sigma\big(R_{\phi}(y_{w},x)-R_{\phi}(y_{l},x)\big)\right)\Big]+\mu_{R}\cdot\mathbb{E}_{(x,y)\sim\mathcal{D}_{R}}\Big[\lvert R_{\phi}(x,y)\rvert^{2}\Big]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{R}(\phi;\mathcal{D}_{R})=-\mathbb{E}_{(x,y_{w},y_{l})\sim\mathcal{D}_{R}}\Big[\log\left(\sigma\big(R_{\phi}(y_{w},x)-R_{\phi}(y_{l},x)\big)\right)\Big]+\mu_{R}\cdot\mathbb{E}_{(x,y)\sim\mathcal{D}_{R}}\Big[\lvert R_{\phi}(x,y)\rvert^{2}\Big],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS1.SSS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A8.SS1.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> is a regularization constant.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS1.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">H.1.2 </span>Cost model</h4>

<div id="A8.SS1.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS1.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the Cost Model (CM), we fine-tune the <span id="A8.SS1.SSS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">LLaMA-2-7B-chat-hf</span> model using a curated jailbreaking dataset <math id="A8.SS1.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{C}</annotation></semantics></math> consisting of prompt–response pairs with absolute labels <math id="A8.SS1.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>. To preserve pretrained knowledge, all but the top six transformer layers (26–31) are frozen. A lightweight classification head produces a scalar logit <math id="A8.SS1.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\psi}(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\psi}(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math>, which is mapped through a sigmoid to yield the probability <math id="A8.SS1.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\psi}(x,y)\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\psi}(x,y)\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> of unsafe content.</p>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS1.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A8.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A8.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle L(\psi)=\underset{i=1}{\overset{N}{\Pi}}P(c_{\psi}(x_{i},y_{i})|x_{i},y_{i},\psi)^{t(x_{i},y_{i})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munderover accent="true" accentunder="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑁</mo></munderover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle L(\psi)=\underset{i=1}{\overset{N}{\Pi}}P(c_{\psi}(x_{i},y_{i})|x_{i},y_{i},\psi)^{t(x_{i},y_{i})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A8.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle l(\psi)=\log{(L(\psi))}=\underset{i=1}{\overset{N}{\sum}}(t(x_{i},y_{i})).P(c_{\psi}(x_{i},y_{i})|x_{i},y_{i},\psi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munderover accent="true" accentunder="true"><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑁</mo></munderover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle l(\psi)=\log{(L(\psi))}=\underset{i=1}{\overset{N}{\sum}}(t(x_{i},y_{i})).P(c_{\psi}(x_{i},y_{i})|x_{i},y_{i},\psi)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A8.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\psi^{*}=\arg\max_{\psi}~L(\psi)=\arg\max_{\psi}~l(\psi)=\arg\max_{\psi}\underset{i=1}{\overset{N}{\sum}}(t(x_{i},y_{i})).\log(P(c_{\psi}(x_{i},y_{i})|x_{i},y_{i},\psi))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>ψ</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>ψ</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>ψ</mi></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munderover accent="true" accentunder="true"><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑁</mo></munderover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\psi^{*}=\arg\max_{\psi}~L(\psi)=\arg\max_{\psi}~l(\psi)=\arg\max_{\psi}\underset{i=1}{\overset{N}{\sum}}(t(x_{i},y_{i})).\log(P(c_{\psi}(x_{i},y_{i})|x_{i},y_{i},\psi))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A8.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\psi^{*}=\arg\min_{\psi}\left(-\underset{i=1}{\overset{N}{\sum}}\sum_{j=1}^{d}t_{j}(x_{i},y_{i}).log(P\left(c_{\psi}(x_{i},y_{i})=t_{j}(x_{i},y_{i})|x_{i},y_{i},\psi)\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>arg</mi><munder><mi>min</mi><mi>ψ</mi></munder><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><munderover accent="true" accentunder="true"><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑁</mo></munderover><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>l</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\psi^{*}=\arg\min_{\psi}\left(-\underset{i=1}{\overset{N}{\sum}}\sum_{j=1}^{d}t_{j}(x_{i},y_{i}).log(P\left(c_{\psi}(x_{i},y_{i})=t_{j}(x_{i},y_{i})|x_{i},y_{i},\psi)\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS1.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS1.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In our work, we consider <math id="A8.SS1.SSS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=2</annotation></semantics></math> which are the two values of <math id="A8.SS1.SSS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\psi}(x_{i},y_{i})\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\psi}(x_{i},y_{i})\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS1.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS1.SSS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Together, these functions allow the RM to provide helpfulness signals via relative preferences, while the CM provides safety signals via absolute judgments.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">H.2 </span>Details of RLHF Training</h3>

<div id="A8.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the RLHF stage, we adopt the training pipeline introduced in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dai et al. (2024)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ouyang et al. (2022)</a></cite>, which combines a reinforcement learning objective with an auxiliary pretraining (PTX) objective. The reward signal is provided by the reward model, regularized by an additional per-token KL divergence penalty to control deviation from a reference model.</p>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Given a prompt <math id="A8.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\sim\mathcal{D}_{\text{prompt}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>prompt</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\sim\mathcal{D}_{\text{prompt}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the current actor <math id="A8.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> generates a response <math id="A8.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="y=a_{1:T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=a_{1:T}</annotation></semantics></math> of length <math id="A8.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>. The reward assigned to each token <math id="A8.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as:</p>
<table id="A8.E25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{t}^{\text{RM}}=\begin{cases}0,&amp;1\leq t&lt;T,\\
R_{\phi}(y,x),&amp;t=T,\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext>RM</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{t}^{\text{RM}}=\begin{cases}0,&amp;1\leq t&lt;T,\\
R_{\phi}(y,x),&amp;t=T,\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A8.E26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E26.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="r_{t}^{\text{KL}}=-\log\frac{\pi_{\theta}(a_{t}\mid x,a_{1:t-1})}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(a_{t}\mid x,a_{1:t-1})},\qquad(1\leq t\leq T)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msubsup><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{t}^{\text{KL}}=-\log\frac{\pi_{\theta}(a_{t}\mid x,a_{1:t-1})}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(a_{t}\mid x,a_{1:t-1})},\qquad(1\leq t\leq T),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A8.E27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{r}_{t}=r_{t}^{\text{RM}}+\beta\cdot r_{t}^{\text{KL}},\qquad(1\leq t\leq T)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext>RM</mtext></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{r}_{t}=r_{t}^{\text{RM}}+\beta\cdot r_{t}^{\text{KL}},\qquad(1\leq t\leq T),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A8.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\text{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\text{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a frozen reference policy and <math id="A8.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> is the KL regularization weight. The RM outputs a sparse reward on the final token only, while the KL term provides dense shaping across all tokens.</p>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The reference model <math id="A8.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\text{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\text{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math> is chosen consistently with the RLHF pipeline: in the first iteration it is the supervised fine-tuned (SFT) model (e.g., Alpaca-7B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">Taori &amp; Hashimoto, 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dai et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, and in later iterations it is the previously fine-tuned checkpoint.</p>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">For optimize the actor with the Proximal Policy Optimization (PPO) algorithm <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Schulman et al., 2017</a>)</cite>. The PPO surrogate objective is:</p>
<table id="A8.E28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}^{\text{RL}}(\theta;\mathcal{D}_{\text{prompt}})=-\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}_{\text{prompt}},y\sim\pi_{\theta}(y|x)}\left[\mathbb{E}_{t}\left[\min\Big(\rho_{t}(\theta)\,\hat{A}_{t},\;\text{clip}(\rho_{t}(\theta),1-\epsilon,1+\epsilon)\,\hat{A}_{t}\Big)\right]\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>RL</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>prompt</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>prompt</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mtext>clip</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}^{\text{RL}}(\theta;\mathcal{D}_{\text{prompt}})=-\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}_{\text{prompt}},y\sim\pi_{\theta}(y|x)}\left[\mathbb{E}_{t}\left[\min\Big(\rho_{t}(\theta)\,\hat{A}_{t},\;\text{clip}(\rho_{t}(\theta),1-\epsilon,1+\epsilon)\,\hat{A}_{t}\Big)\right]\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="A8.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\rho_{t}(\theta)=\frac{\pi_{\theta}(a_{t}\mid a_{1:t-1},x)}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(a_{t}\mid a_{1:t-1},x)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{t}(\theta)=\frac{\pi_{\theta}(a_{t}\mid a_{1:t-1},x)}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(a_{t}\mid a_{1:t-1},x)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS2.p4.3" class="ltx_p">is the importance weight, <math id="A8.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> is the PPO clipping threshold, <math id="A8.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\text{old}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\text{old}}</annotation></semantics></math> are parameters from the previous update, and <math id="A8.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{A}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{A}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is the token-level advantage estimated with generalized advantage estimation (GAE) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Schulman et al., 2015</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Alongside the RL objective, including a PTX loss to regularize against catastrophic forgetting. Since the original pretraining data is unavailable, then compute this term on the supervised fine-tuning dataset <math id="A8.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\text{SFT}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>SFT</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\text{SFT}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A8.E29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}^{\text{PTX}}(\theta;\mathcal{D}_{\text{SFT}})=-\mathbb{E}_{(x,y)\sim\mathcal{D}_{\text{SFT}}}\big[\log\pi_{\theta}(y|x)\big]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>PTX</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>SFT</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>SFT</mtext></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}^{\text{PTX}}(\theta;\mathcal{D}_{\text{SFT}})=-\mathbb{E}_{(x,y)\sim\mathcal{D}_{\text{SFT}}}\big[\log\pi_{\theta}(y|x)\big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">The combined RLHF loss is then expressed as:</p>
<table id="A8.E30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}^{\text{RLHF}}(\theta;\mathcal{D}_{\text{prompt}},\mathcal{D}_{\text{SFT}})=\mathcal{L}^{\text{RL}}(\theta;\mathcal{D}_{\text{prompt}})+\gamma\cdot\mathcal{L}^{\text{PTX}}(\theta;\mathcal{D}_{\text{SFT}})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>RLHF</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>prompt</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>SFT</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>RL</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>prompt</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>PTX</mtext></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>SFT</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}^{\text{RLHF}}(\theta;\mathcal{D}_{\text{prompt}},\mathcal{D}_{\text{SFT}})=\mathcal{L}^{\text{RL}}(\theta;\mathcal{D}_{\text{prompt}})+\gamma\cdot\mathcal{L}^{\text{PTX}}(\theta;\mathcal{D}_{\text{SFT}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS2.p6.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A8.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> balances reinforcement and PTX objectives.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">H.3 </span>Training Objectives: Safe-RLHF (reference) vs. CS-RLHF (ours)</h3>

<div id="A8.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Reference (Safe-RLHF)</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dai et al., 2024</a>)</cite> casts alignment as a constrained optimization and solves it with an <em id="A8.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">adaptive Lagrangian multiplier</em>. Their surrogate PPO losses and update rules include a normalization by <math id="A8.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1+\lambda_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1+\lambda_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and a separate dual-variable update. We follow their <em id="A8.SS3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">RLHF mechanics</em> (tokenization, KL shaping, GAE, PPO) but <em id="A8.SS3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">remove</em> the dual variable in favor of a deterministic penalty.</p>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CS-RLHF with a fixed-<math id="A8.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> ReLU penalty</span></p>
</div>
<section id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Token-level signals</h5>

<div id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a prompt <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\sim\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\sim\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> and a policy rollout <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="y=a_{1:T}\sim\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=a_{1:T}\sim\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|x)</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Reward model (sparse at the last token):</span></p>
<table id="A8.E31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{\text{RM}}_{t}=\begin{cases}0,&amp;1\leq t&lt;T,\\
R_{\phi}(y,x),&amp;t=T.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext>RM</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{\text{RM}}_{t}=\begin{cases}0,&amp;1\leq t&lt;T,\\
R_{\phi}(y,x),&amp;t=T.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Per-token KL shaping (as in RLHF):</span></p>
<table id="A8.E32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E32.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="r^{\text{KL}}_{t}\;=\;-\log\frac{\pi_{\theta}(a_{t}\mid x,a_{1:t-1})}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(a_{t}\mid x,a_{1:t-1})}\quad(1\leq t\leq T)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.058em">=</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{\text{KL}}_{t}\;=\;-\log\frac{\pi_{\theta}(a_{t}\mid x,a_{1:t-1})}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(a_{t}\mid x,a_{1:t-1})}\quad(1\leq t\leq T).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Shaped reward used by PPO:</span></p>
<table id="A8.E33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{r}_{t}\;=\;r^{\text{RM}}_{t}\;+\;\beta\,r^{\text{KL}}_{t}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext>RM</mtext></msubsup><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{r}_{t}\;=\;r^{\text{RM}}_{t}\;+\;\beta\,r^{\text{KL}}_{t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Cost model (sparse at the last token):</span></p>
<table id="A8.E34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{\text{CM}}_{t}=\begin{cases}0,&amp;1\leq t&lt;T,\\
C_{\psi}(y,x),&amp;t=T.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext>CM</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{\text{CM}}_{t}=\begin{cases}0,&amp;1\leq t&lt;T,\\
C_{\psi}(y,x),&amp;t=T.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">We keep the cost channel separate; we do <span id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">not</span> introduce a per-token cost KL term.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Advantages (GAE)</h5>

<div id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{A}^{r}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{A}^{r}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{A}^{c}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{A}^{c}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> denote GAE advantages computed from the shaped reward <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{r}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{r}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and the sparse cost <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{\text{CM}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext>CM</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{\text{CM}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively (value/critic baselines are fit in the standard way).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">PPO surrogates</h5>

<div id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">With importance ratio <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\rho_{t}(\theta)=\tfrac{\pi_{\theta}(a_{t}\mid x,a_{1:t-1})}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(a_{t}\mid x,a_{1:t-1})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{t}(\theta)=\tfrac{\pi_{\theta}(a_{t}\mid x,a_{1:t-1})}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(a_{t}\mid x,a_{1:t-1})}</annotation></semantics></math> and clip ratio <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Reward path:</span></p>
<table id="A8.E35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{R}^{\text{PPO}}({\theta;\mathcal{D}_{\text{prompt}}})=-\,\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\\
\mathcal{D}_{\text{prompt}},\;y\sim\pi_{\theta}}\!\Bigg[\mathbb{E}_{t}\;\Bigg[\min\!\Big(\rho_{t}(\theta)\,\hat{A}^{r}_{t},\;\mathrm{clip}(\rho_{t}(\theta),\,1-\varepsilon,\,1+\varepsilon)\,\hat{A}^{r}_{t}\Big)\Bigg]\Bigg]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>R</mi><mtext>PPO</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>prompt</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>prompt</mtext></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.653em;" width="1.653em"><mi>min</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>clip</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{R}^{\text{PPO}}({\theta;\mathcal{D}_{\text{prompt}}})=-\,\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\\
\mathcal{D}_{\text{prompt}},\;y\sim\pi_{\theta}}\!\Bigg[\mathbb{E}_{t}\;\Bigg[\min\!\Big(\rho_{t}(\theta)\,\hat{A}^{r}_{t},\;\mathrm{clip}(\rho_{t}(\theta),\,1-\varepsilon,\,1+\varepsilon)\,\hat{A}^{r}_{t}\Big)\Bigg]\Bigg]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Cost path:</span></p>
<table id="A8.E36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{C}^{\text{PPO}}({\theta;\mathcal{D}_{\text{prompt}}})=-\,\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\\
\mathcal{D}_{\text{prompt}},\;y\sim\pi_{\theta}}\!\Bigg[\mathbb{E}_{t}\;\Bigg[\min\!\Big(\rho_{t}(\theta)\,\hat{A}^{c}_{t},\;\mathrm{clip}(\rho_{t}(\theta),\,1-\varepsilon,\,1+\varepsilon)\,\hat{A}^{c}_{t}\Big)\Bigg]\Bigg]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>C</mi><mtext>PPO</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>prompt</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>prompt</mtext></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.653em;" width="1.653em"><mi>min</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>clip</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{C}^{\text{PPO}}({\theta;\mathcal{D}_{\text{prompt}}})=-\,\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\\
\mathcal{D}_{\text{prompt}},\;y\sim\pi_{\theta}}\!\Bigg[\mathbb{E}_{t}\;\Bigg[\min\!\Big(\rho_{t}(\theta)\,\hat{A}^{c}_{t},\;\mathrm{clip}(\rho_{t}(\theta),\,1-\varepsilon,\,1+\varepsilon)\,\hat{A}^{c}_{t}\Big)\Bigg]\Bigg]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Batch-level expected-cost estimator and hinge</h5>

<div id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let the safety threshold be <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>. On each minibatch <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A8.E37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathcal{J}}_{C}(\theta)\;=\;\frac{1}{|B|}\sum_{(x,y)\in B}\big(C_{\psi}(y,x)-d\big),\qquad h(\theta)\;=\;\max\big(\widehat{\mathcal{J}}_{C}(\theta),\,0\big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn> 0</mn><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathcal{J}}_{C}(\theta)\;=\;\frac{1}{|B|}\sum_{(x,y)\in B}\big(C_{\psi}(y,x)-d\big),\qquad h(\theta)\;=\;\max\big(\widehat{\mathcal{J}}_{C}(\theta),\,0\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">so the cost term activates <span id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">only when</span> the batch mean cost exceeds <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">PTX (supervised) regularization</h5>

<div id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As in RLHF, we include the PTX loss <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{PTX}}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>PTX</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{PTX}}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> computed over the SFT data with coefficient <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">CS-RLHF objective (no dual variable)</h5>

<div id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A8.E38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{\;\mathcal{L}_{\text{CS}}(\theta)\;=\;\mathcal{L}_{R}^{\text{PPO}}(\theta)\;+\;\lambda\;\mathbb{I}\!\big\{\widehat{\mathcal{J}}_{C}(\theta)&gt;0\big\}\;\mathcal{L}_{C}^{\text{PPO}}(\theta)\;+\;\gamma\,\mathcal{L}_{\text{PTX}}(\theta)\;}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>CS</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>R</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>PPO</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mi>λ</mi><mpadded style="width:0.219em;" width="0.219em"><mi>𝕀</mi></mpadded><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>C</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">}</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>C</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>PPO</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mi>γ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>PTX</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{\;\mathcal{L}_{\text{CS}}(\theta)\;=\;\mathcal{L}_{R}^{\text{PPO}}(\theta)\;+\;\lambda\;\mathbb{I}\!\big\{\widehat{\mathcal{J}}_{C}(\theta)&gt;0\big\}\;\mathcal{L}_{C}^{\text{PPO}}(\theta)\;+\;\gamma\,\mathcal{L}_{\text{PTX}}(\theta)\;}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We minimize <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{CS}}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>CS</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{CS}}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> with standard PPO updates. The gradient takes the form</p>
<table id="A8.E39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E39.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\text{CS}}(\theta)=\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{R}^{\text{PPO}}(\theta)\;+\;\lambda\,\mathbb{I}\!\big\{\widehat{\mathcal{J}}_{C}(\theta)&gt;0\big\}\,\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{C}^{\text{PPO}}(\theta)\;+\;\gamma\,\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\text{PTX}}(\theta)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>CS</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>R</mi><mtext>PPO</mtext></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mi>λ</mi><mpadded style="width:0.219em;" width="0.219em"><mi>𝕀</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>C</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>C</mi><mtext>PPO</mtext></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mi>γ</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>PTX</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\text{CS}}(\theta)=\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{R}^{\text{PPO}}(\theta)\;+\;\lambda\,\mathbb{I}\!\big\{\widehat{\mathcal{J}}_{C}(\theta)&gt;0\big\}\,\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{C}^{\text{PPO}}(\theta)\;+\;\gamma\,\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\text{PTX}}(\theta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Thus, no factor <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tfrac{1}{1+\lambda_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tfrac{1}{1+\lambda_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math> appears and there is no dual-variable update. Safety enforcement is <em id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">deterministic</em>: whenever the expected cost in the batch exceeds <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>, the cost PPO gradient is applied with fixed weight <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>; otherwise it is zero. This directly implements the hinge <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{ReLU}(\mathcal{J}_{C})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ReLU</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{ReLU}(\mathcal{J}_{C})</annotation></semantics></math> at the batch level while retaining PPO’s variance-reduction and clipping behavior.</p>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p4.1" class="ltx_p">This yields, predictable enforcement of the safety constraint without oscillations from dual-variable dynamics, while maintaining the practical PPO training loop.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A9" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix I </span>Details of the Supplementary Experiments</h2>

<section id="A9.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">I.1 </span>Hyper-Parameters</h3>

<div id="A9.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A9.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Below are the hyper-parameters utilized during the CS-RLHF training.
Tables <a href="#A9.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ I.1 Hyper-Parameters ‣ Appendix I Details of the Supplementary Experiments ‣ Certifiable Safe RLHF: Fixed-Penalty Constraint Optimization for Safer Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, <a href="#A9.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ I.1 Hyper-Parameters ‣ Appendix I Details of the Supplementary Experiments ‣ Certifiable Safe RLHF: Fixed-Penalty Constraint Optimization for Safer Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, and <a href="#A9.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ I.1 Hyper-Parameters ‣ Appendix I Details of the Supplementary Experiments ‣ Certifiable Safe RLHF: Fixed-Penalty Constraint Optimization for Safer Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A9.T5" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5: </span>Hyper-parameters of CS-RLHF policy training.</figcaption>
<table id="A9.T5.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A9.T5.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A9.T5.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="A9.T5.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hyper-parameter</span></td>
<td id="A9.T5.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="A9.T5.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CS-RLHF</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A9.T5.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A9.T5.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">epochs</td>
<td id="A9.T5.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">1</td></tr>
<tr id="A9.T5.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A9.T5.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_l ltx_border_r">max length</td>
<td id="A9.T5.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r">512</td></tr>
<tr id="A9.T5.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A9.T5.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_l ltx_border_r">temperature</td>
<td id="A9.T5.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r">1.0</td></tr>
<tr id="A9.T5.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A9.T5.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_l ltx_border_r">top-<math id="A9.T5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A9.T5.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r">1.0</td></tr>
<tr id="A9.T5.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A9.T5.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_l ltx_border_r">num return sequences</td>
<td id="A9.T5.2.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r">1</td></tr>
<tr id="A9.T5.2.7" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A9.T5.2.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_l ltx_border_r">repetition penalty</td>
<td id="A9.T5.2.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r">1.0</td></tr>
<tr id="A9.T5.2.8" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A9.T5.2.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_l ltx_border_r">per-device prompt batch size</td>
<td id="A9.T5.2.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r">4</td></tr>
<tr id="A9.T5.2.9" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A9.T5.2.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_l ltx_border_r">per-device train batch size</td>
<td id="A9.T5.2.9.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r">4</td></tr>
<tr id="A9.T5.2.10" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A9.T5.2.10.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_l ltx_border_r">gradient accumulation steps</td>
